/* The question bank: every question, picture, map, flag, dish, airport, fact and Majority Rules question, and how
   they become the bank's rows (buildSeedBank). Moved out of classic.html on 21 Nov 2026 (the owner: Classic is
   retired; the bank shouldn't live in it).
     node scripts/export-bank.js   writes party/data/bank.json and party/public/bank.json from it
   Plain JavaScript: in a browser it gives its names to the page (classic.html still loads it, to draw the maps for
   scripts/export-maps.js); in Node, require() it. Bump BUILD.v and SEED_VERSION (and version.json) with every change.
   How the content is written: docs/CONTENT-RULES.md. */

function hash(str){ let h = 5381; for(let i=0;i<str.length;i++) h = ((h<<5)+h+str.charCodeAt(i))|0; return 'q'+(h>>>0).toString(36); }

/* ==========================================================================
   0. BUILD STAMP
   ==========================================================================
   The footer on the home screen reads from here and nowhere else, so the
   version and the date can never end up disagreeing with each other. There is
   no build step in a single HTML file — nothing updates this on its own, so
   BUMP BOTH FIELDS whenever you change the app. A date that has quietly gone
   stale is worse than no date at all.

   Deriving it from document.lastModified was the obvious alternative and is a
   trap: copying the file to another laptop resets the timestamp, so a build
   from months ago would announce itself as updated today.
   ========================================================================== */
const BUILD = { v:'3.76', date:'21 Nov 2026', author:'Thierry Boulos', year:2026 };

